    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1555">

                <pb facs="1254" n="1138" xml:id="pg1138"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.00/393.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 9, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Porras and Díaz both absent in the interior, but the leaders of both parties have
                    to-day affirmed to me over their signatures that Porras and Díaz both desire
                    American supervision of registration and election. This I believe to be true.
                    The written statements were signed for Porras by Mendoza, Valdés and Chiari; for
                    Díaz by President Arosemena. I recommend our acquiescence, and believe the
                    committee as described could devise suitable measures in the manner indicated,
                    as Governor Thatcher is on leave. President Arosemena has asked me by a note
                    just received to urge my Government to accede to the request of the Government
                    of Panama.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodge.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
